<article class="env-lemma" id="092G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/092G">Lemma <span data-tag="092G">15.106.6</span>.</a> A product of fields is an absolutely flat ring. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $K_ i$ be a family of fields. If $f = (f_ i) \in \prod K_ i$, then the ideal generated by $f$ is the same as the ideal generated by the idempotent $e = (e_ i)$ with $e_ i = 0, 1$ according to whether $f_ i$ is $0$ or not. Thus $D(f) = D(e)$ is open and closed and we conclude by Lemma <a href="/tag/092F" data-tag="092F">15.106.5</a> and Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/04MG" data-tag="04MG">10.26.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>